hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17084","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Ibn al-Munkadir, from Abu Ayyub, from Maslamah ibn Mukhallad, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever covers a Muslim in this world, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will cover him in this world and the Hereafter, and whoever relieves a distressed one, Allah will relieve from him a distress of the distresses of the Day of Resurrection, and whoever is in the need of his brother, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will be in his need."
"17085","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I read to my father this hadith: Abbad ibn Abbad and Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Makhul, that Uqbah - Ibn Abi Adi said: came to Maslamah ibn Mukhallad in Misr, while between him and the doorkeeper was something, and he heard his voice so he gave him permission - said: I did not come to you visiting, but I came to you for a need. Do you remember the day - Abbad said in his hadith: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever knows an evil deed of his brother and covers it, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will cover him thereby on the Day of Resurrection? So he said: Yes. So he said: For this I came. Ibn Abi Adi said in his hadith: Uqbah ibn Amir rode to Maslamah ibn Mukhallad while he was governor over Misr."
